---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import NextProject from '../../../components/NextProject.astro';
import Icon from '../../../Icons/components/Icons.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Kula Design System — Lisandro Eijo" showNav={false}>
  <div class="cs__page">

    <nav class="topbar">
      <a href="/work" class="back-link">
        <Icon name="arrow-left" size="sm" /> 
        Work
      </a>
      
      <button id="lockBtn" class="badge">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 10 12" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="width:10px;height:12px;">
          <rect x="0.5" y="5" width="9" height="6.5" rx="1.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.8"/>
          <path d="M2 5V3.5a3 3 0 0 1 6 0V5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.8" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        </svg>
        NDA protected
      </button>
      
    </nav>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="col-md">
        <header class="cs__header">
          <p class="cs__meta">Relyance AI · 2024–2025</p>
          <h1 class="cs__title">Kula Design System</h1>
          <p class="cs__tagline">
            Building a scalable design system from scratch for a B2B data-privacy SaaS platform.
          </p>
          <div class="cs__tags">
            <span class="badge">Design Systems</span>
            <span class="badge">Component Library</span>
            <span class="badge">Figma</span>
            <span class="badge">Design Tokens</span>
            <span class="badge">Documentation</span>
            <span class="badge">Typography</span>
            <span class="badge">Data visualization</span>
            <span class="badge">Contribution guidelines</span>
          </div>
        </header>

      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="cards__container">
          <div class="card">
            <p class="card__title">Role</p>
            <p class="card__body">DS Lead</p> 
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <p class="card__title">Project duration</p>
            <p class="card__body">8 months</p> 
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <p class="card__title">Components</p>
            <p class="card__body">~50</p> 
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <p class="card__title">Stack</p>
            <p class="card__body">Figma + React.js</p> 
          </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <p class="cs__meta">Problem</p>
      <h3 class="section__title">A product without a system.</h3>
      <p class="section__tagline">
         When I joined Relyance AI, the product had screen designs with UI elements but no systematized components. There was no design system file. Each screen was treated in isolation, with visual elements that were inconsistent with one another. <br>
         Engineering was already using a component library based on Google's Material 3, completely disconnected from the visual design. The gap between what was designed and what was implemented was evident.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <p class="cs__meta">Process</p>
      <h3 class="section__title">Foundations first</h3> 
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-md">
          <p class="section__tagline">
            I started with an audit of the live product and design files against WCAG 2.1 AA standards, which surfaced contrast failures, inconsistent typography, and color usage. These findings helped define the priorities and foundations for the work ahead.
          </p>
          <p>The process followed a clear progression: first, establishing the foundations and defining the necessary design tokens; then, building the core components; and finally, creating product-specific elements to address the needs of the platform.</p>  
          
        </div>
        <div class="col-md">
          <div class="img-container">
            <img src="/images/usecase-kula/from-tokens-to-business-components.png" class="centered" alt="Diagram showing Kula's component architecture: design tokens (typography, color, spacing) flowing into a basic component, which then composes into a more complex business component">
  
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>

      
    </section>
     <section class="section challenges">
      <p class="cs__meta">Challenges</p>
      <h3 class="section__title">Constraints That Shaped the System</h3>
      <p class="body-text">
        Every design system runs into some version of the same problems: adoption, documentation, and scale. Kula was no exception, and each challenge had its own resolution arc.
      </p>
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-lg">

          <div class="challenges__section">
            <div class="challenges__block list">
              <div class="list__number">.01</div>
              <div class="list__content">
                <h4 class="challenges__title">Adoption</h4>
                <p class="challenges__body">
                  Engineering adoption was willing but costly. There was no dedicated resource on the engineering side to implement the design system — every developer was absorbing it while still shipping features. Existing technical debt created constant friction. The system gained traction, but slowly, and always in competition with delivery pressure.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="challenges__block list">
              <div class="list__number">.02</div>
              <div class="list__content">
                <h4 class="challenges__title"> Documentation</h4>
                <p class="challenges__body">
                 Storybook was explored as a bridge between design and code, but was ruled out due to technical constraints on the engineering side. Confluence was set up as an alternative, but never made it into the developers' actual workflow. Documentation ended up living primarily inside Figma — a pragmatic decision given the constraints, but one that limited its reach on the engineering side. 
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="challenges__block list">
              <div class="list__number">.03</div>
              <div class="list__content">
                <h4 class="challenges__title">Scale</h4>
                <p class="challenges__body">
                  As the system grew, the main Figma file accumulated enough pages to become slow and hard to navigate. The decision was to split icons and data visualization into separate files, linked back to the core through Figma libraries. The impact on working speed was immediate.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>  
        </div>
        <div class="col-sm">
          <div class="img-container">
            <img src="/images/usecase-kula/Three__pillars.svg" class="centered" alt="Triangle diagram showing the three core challenges of Kula in tension: Documentation, Adoption, and Scale, with a center point representing the balance between them"/>

          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-md">
          <p class="cs__meta">Look & feel</p>
          <h3 class="section__title">A system that grows with the product</h3> 
          <p class="section__tagline">
            How Kula feels in practice: clear and precise, built from tokens, components, and patterns that stay consistent at every scale.
          </p>

        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="img-container in-rows">
        <img src="/images/usecase-kula/kula-tokens.png" class="centered" alt="Typography palette for the Kula design system">
        <img src="/images/usecase-kula/kula-icons.png" class="centered" alt="Typography palette for the Kula design system">
        <img src="/images/usecase-kula/kula-base-components.png" class="centered" alt="Typography palette for the Kula design system">
        <img src="/images/usecase-kula/Kula-business-components.png" class="centered" alt="Typography palette for the Kula design system">
      </div>
    </section>   
    <section class="section">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm">
          <p class="cs__meta">Outcome</p>
          <h3 class="section__title">The impact</h3> 
          <p class="section__tagline">
           The Design System enabled a more consistent, scalable and efficient product, accelerating development and improving the overall user experience.
          </p>

        </div>
        <div class="col-lg">
          <div class="impact-card__container">
            <div class="impact-card">
              <img src="/images/usecase-kula/icon-launch.svg" class="centered" alt="rocket icon representing speed and acceleration">
              <p class="metric">40%</p>
              <p class="metric-label">Faster Delivery</p>
            </div>
            <div class="impact-card">
              <img src="/images/usecase-kula/icon-consistency.svg" class="centered" alt="icon representing consistency and trust">
              <p class="metric">100%</p>
              <p class="metric-label">Design Consistency</p>
            </div>
            <div class="impact-card">
              <img src="/images/usecase-kula/icon-team.svg" class="centered" alt="icon representing team collaboration">
              <p class="metric">60%</p>
              <p class="metric-label">Team Adoption</p>
            </div>
            
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
      <h4>What I have learned</h4>
      <div class="row align-center">
        <div class="col-md">
          <p class="display-big"> A design system <strong> without an adoption strategy is only half a product</strong></p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md">
          <p>Kula is one of the most complex design systems I've built. It's also the first in which I faced a problem hard to ignore: the distance between what gets documented and what actually gets adopted.</p>  
        </div>
      </div>
      
      
    </section> 
    
    <NextProject
      title="Smart Saving"
      subtitle="Turns saving into a two-minute setup."
      link="https://www.behance.net/gallery/245960381/Smart-Savings-Bank-app-feature"
    />

  </div>
</BaseLayout>
<style lang="scss">
    @use "../../../styles/tokens" as *;
    @use "../../../styles/typography"as *;
   
    img.centered{
      margin: 0 auto;
    }
    .img-container{
      height: 100%;  
      display: flex;
      justify-content: center;
      &.in-rows{
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 0;
      }
    }
    //  page Layout
    .cs{
      &__page {
        background-image: url("/images/usecase-kula/Kula--hero.png");
        background-size: 60%;
        background-position: top right;
        background-repeat: no-repeat;
        max-width: 1200px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 4rem 0.5rem 8rem;
        animation: fadeUp 0.4s ease forwards;
        @media screen and (max-width: $bp-lg) {
          background-image: none;
          padding: 4rem 1rem 6rem;
        }
      }
      &__meta{
        @extend .label--sm;
        color: $neutral-400;
        margin-bottom: $space-2 ;
      }
      &__title{
        font-size: 2.5rem;
        margin-bottom: $space-4;
      }
      &__tagline{        
        font-size: $font-size-body-big;
        font-weight: 300;
        line-height: 1.65;
        color:$neutral-500;
      }
      &__header { 
        margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
        max-width: 900px;
      }
      &__tags {
        display: flex;
        gap: 8px;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        margin-top: 2rem;
      }
    }

    // Topbar
    .topbar {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      align-items: center;
      margin-bottom: 4rem;
      a {
        display: inline-flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 6px;
        font-size: 13px;
        text-decoration: none;
        transition: opacity 0.15s;
      }
      a:hover { opacity: 1; }
    }

    .lock-tag {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 5px;
      font-size: 11px;
      border: 1px solid currentColor;
      border-radius: 20px;
      padding: 4px 10px;
      letter-spacing: 0.3px;
      opacity: 0.25;
    }
    

    // Content
    hr {
      border: none;
      border-top: 1px solid currentColor;
      opacity: 0.1;
      margin: 3rem 0;
    }
    
    .section {
      margin-bottom: 3.5rem; 

      p{
        color: $neutral-500;
        &.display-big{
          font-size: $font-size-display-big;
          font-weight: $font-weight-light;
          color: $neutral-600;  
          margin: $space-6 0;
          strong{
            color:$color-accent;
          }
        }
      }
      .cs__meta{
        color: $color-accent;

      }
      &__label {
        @extend .label--xs;
        color:$color-accent;
        margin-bottom: $space-2;
      }
      &__title{
        margin-bottom: $space-4;
      }
      &__tagline{
        margin-bottom:$space-4;
        font-size: $font-size-body-big;

      }
      &__body {
        font-size: $font-size-body-small;
        line-height: 1.8;
        font-weight: 300;
        color: $neutral-500;
        margin-bottom: $space-6;
      }
      h4.section__title{
        margin-bottom: $space-1;
      }
    }
    
    // cards

    .cards__container{
      display: flex;
      margin: $space-8 0;
      @media screen and (max-width: $bp-sm) {
        flex-direction: column;
        padding: $space-4 0;
      }
    }
    .cs__page{

      .card{
        border-width: 1px 0 1px 1px; 
        border-style: solid;
        border-color: $neutral-100;
        padding: $space-4 $space-6;
        background-color: $color-bg;
        @media screen and (max-width: $bp-sm) {
          border-width: 1px 1px 0 1px;
          padding: $space-4;
        }
        &:first-child{
          border-radius: $space-4 0 0 $space-4;
          @media screen and (max-width: $bp-sm) {
            border-radius: $space-4 $space-4 0 0;
          }
        }
        &:last-child{
          border-right: 1px solid $neutral-100;
          border-radius: 0 $space-4 $space-4 0;
          @media screen and (max-width: $bp-sm) {
            border-radius: 0 0 $space-4 $space-4;
            border-bottom: 1px solid $neutral-100;
          }
        }
        &__title{
          @extend .label--xs;
        }
        &__body{
          font-weight: $font-weight-black;
          color:$color-primary;
        }

      }
    }
    .list{
      display: flex;
      gap:$space-3;
      &__number{
        font-size: $font-size-title-large;
        font-weight: $font-weight-black;
        color: $neutral-100;
      }
      &__content{
        margin-top: $space-2;
      }
    }
    .challenges{
      &__block{
        margin: $space-6 0;
      }
      &__title{
        font-size: $font-size-h4;
        margin-bottom: $space-1;
      }
      &__body{
        font-size: $font-size-body;
        color: $neutral-600
      }
    }
    .impact-card{
      flex: 1 1 0;
      text-align: center;
      padding: $space-6;
      border-radius: $radius-lg;
      background-color: $neutral-50;
      border: 1px solid $neutral-100;
      @media screen and (max-width: $bp-sm) {
        width: 100%;
        max-width: 280px;
      }
      &__container{
        display: flex;
        gap: $space-6;
        margin-bottom: $space-6;
        @media screen and (max-width: $bp-sm) {
          flex-direction: column;
          align-items: center;
          text-align: center;
        }
        
      }
      img{
        width: 80px;
        height: 80px;
      }
      .metric{
        font-size: $font-size-title-large;
        font-weight: $font-weight-black;
        color:$color-accent;
        margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
      }
      .metric-label{
        font-size: $font-size-body-big;
        color:$color-primary;
      }
    }
    
    @keyframes fadeUp {
      from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(12px); }
      to   { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }
    }
  </style>

  <script>
    function getCookie(name) {
      return document.cookie.split('; ').find(r => r.startsWith(name + '='))?.split('=')[1];
    }

    if (getCookie('cs_unlocked') !== 'true') {
      window.location.href = '/work/kula';
    }

    document.getElementById('lockBtn').addEventListener('click', () => {
      document.cookie = "cs_unlocked=; path=/; max-age=0; SameSite=Strict";
      window.location.href = '/work/kula';
    });

</script>